content.text:
Here is what was going wrong and what we changed.

**Cause:** `ProductPage` was `async` and awaited `getInventory()` before returning any JSX. That function uses `connection()`, so the whole route waited on that work. Nothing rendered until it finished—including the fixed heading.

**Change:** The page is now a normal (non-async) component that always renders the `<h1>` right away. Only the stock/price block lives in a separate async `InventoryDetails` component inside `Suspense`, so that part can stream in later. `metadata.title` is set to `Premium Widget` so the tab title matches without waiting on inventory.

The production build reports `/product` as **Partial Prerender**: static HTML for the shell plus streamed dynamic content, which matches this layout.

```1:36:/vercel/sandbox/app/product/page.tsx
import { Suspense } from 'react'
import type { Metadata } from 'next'
import { getInventory } from '@/lib/data'

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Premium Widget',
}

async function InventoryDetails() {
  const inventory = await getInventory()

  return (
    <>
      <p>{inventory.count} in stock</p>
      <p>Price: ${inventory.price}</p>
    </>
  )
}

export default function ProductPage() {
  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Premium Widget</h1>
      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading inventory…</p>}>
        <InventoryDetails />
      </Suspense>
    </main>
  )
}
```

If you want the fallback to be subtler (e.g. gray skeleton lines instead of “Loading inventory…”), say how you’d like it to look and we can adjust it.

